Package: studygate
Type: Package
Title: Study-Specific Validation Rules and Programmer Guidance for Clinical Analysis Datasets
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Param", "Madan", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "86084060+parammadan@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Turns a versioned, study-specific YAML specification into
    deterministic validation checks for ADaM-style analysis datasets
    (for example ADSL and ADAE), and explains every finding: the affected
    records, expected versus observed values, why it matters, how to
    investigate it, and the rule it came from. The same rule set drives
    validation, release gating and programmer guidance, so a new study
    reuses the engine by supplying a new specification. Data are never
    modified. An independent research prototype: not a validated or
    regulatory-certified tool and not a CDISC conformance checker. Example
    data are synthetic.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: jsonlite, tools, utils, yaml
Suggests: haven, knitr, rmarkdown, testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr
